From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 15 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] system/audio.h: include string.h for strdup()

audio_device_address_to_parameter() is a static inline in this header and
calls strdup(), but the header only includes stdio.h, so every consumer
compiled as C picks up an implicit declaration. GCC 15 defaults to -std=gnu23,
where that is an error rather than a warning, and libhybris stops building:

    system/audio.h:1001:12: error: implicit declaration of function 'strdup';
                            did you mean 'strcmp'? [-Wimplicit-function-declaration]
    system/audio.h:1001:12: error: returning 'int' from a function with return
                            type 'char *' makes pointer from integer without a cast

Include what the header uses.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 system/audio.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/system/audio.h
+++ b/system/audio.h
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #include <stdbool.h>
 #include <stdint.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
+#include <string.h>
 #include <sys/cdefs.h>
 #include <sys/types.h>
 
